Having received some responses indicating interest, here is how to modify
NH3.1.3 for the Macintosh to get "classic" num pad (i.e. jkl for
jump/kick/loot, 5+direction to run) behavior:

Caveats:
1)  This modification has not been discussed with any member of the
DevTeam, and will not be supported by them.  Use it at your own risk.

2)  ResEdit modification of any application on the Macintosh is risky,
especially if you are not to sure of what you are doing (I sort of closed
my eyes and hoped, but having the source and working with my own compile
increased my confidence level amazingly :-)


That being said, the modification is really easy.

1)  Copy your NetHack application to a safe place (in case you screw up).

2)  Open the application using ResEdit.

3)  Find the resource named "Nump" (it contains the num pad mappings).

4)  Delete it.

5)  Quit ResEdit, saving the changes to NetHack

6)  Edit your NetHack Defaults file, using TeachText or other FLAT ASCII
editor (if you use word, make sure you save as text, _not_ normal)

7)  Add OPTIONS=number_pad to the NetHack Defaults file

8)  Quit and save NetHack Defaults

9)  HACK AWAY!!!!!!!!!!!

